From cad8cec011c35fd9ae7878eb2e4944fc8ec39448 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:40:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/53] Local workflow files from the host app in embedded
 builds

The web build has no file system, so the host app reads ~/.warp/workflows and the workspace's
.warp/workflows and hands their text over (`window.warpPanelWorkflows`); Warp parses the YAML like
desktop does and loads the workflows as local user workflows. Ctrl+R gets the local workflows
source and its "workflows:" filter without Warp Drive, and the workflow card hides the
environment variables row (a Warp Drive feature).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
